{"tool_name":"svim-asm","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"svim-asm","identifiers":["doi:10.1038/s41587-020-0503-6","doi:10.1101/2020.10.27.356907"],"license":"GNU General Public License v3.0","summary":"Svim-asm is a fork of the sv caller svim for genome-genome alignments.","home_url":"https://github.com/eldariont/svim-asm","keywords":["Benchmarking","Chromosomes, Human","Deep Learning","Genome, Human","Genomics","HLA Antigens","Haploidy","High-Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing","Humans","Nanopore Sequencing","Sequence Analysis, DNA"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":4},"biotools":{"id":"svim-asm","home":"http://github.com/eldariont/svim-asm","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Structural variant detection from haploid and diploid genome assemblies.\n\nSVIM-asm - Structural variant identification method (Assembly edition).\n\nSVIM-asm (pronounced SWIM-assem) is a structural variant caller for haploid or diploid genome-genome alignments. It analyzes a given sorted BAM file (preferably from minimap2) and detects five different variant classes between the query assembly and the reference: deletions, insertions, tandem and interspersed duplications and inversions.","addition_date":"2021-01-18T11:21:50Z","last_update_date":"2021-02-24T13:08:48Z","biotools_curie":"biotools:svim-asm","credit":[{"email":"vingron@molgen.mpg.de","name":"Martin Vingron","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Genome assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0525"},{"term":"Genotyping","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3196"},{"term":"Variant calling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3227"}]}],"name":"SVIM-asm","owner":"zsmag19","publication":[{"doi":"10.1101/2020.10.27.356907"}],"topic":[{"term":"DNA polymorphism","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2885"},{"term":"Genotype and phenotype","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0625"},{"term":"Sequenc